  "question": {
    "text": "Two iron solid discs of negligible thickness have radii $R_1$ and $R_2$ and moment of intertia $I_1$ and $I_2$, respectively. For $R_2=2 R_1$, the ratio of $I_1$ and $I_2$ would be $1 / x$, where $\\mathrm{x}=$ ________ -",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/LCWd07a_Ujs8S8XbMrPQB-ZSMFPXmLzDyKzoBa3c_qI.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\nGiven $R_2=2 R_1$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& M_1=\\sigma \\times \\pi R_1^2=M_o \\\\\n& M_2=\\sigma \\times \\pi R_2^2=M_o \\\\\n& M_2=\\sigma \\times \\pi R_2^2=\\sigma \\times \\pi\\left[2 R_1\\right]^2=\\sigma \\times 4 \\pi R_1^2=4 M_o\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\frac{I_1}{I_2}=\\frac{\\frac{M_1 R_1^2}{2}}{\\frac{M_2 R_2^2}{2}}=\\frac{M_1 R_1^2}{M_2 R_2^2}=\\frac{1}{4} \\times \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{16}$",
    "image": null
  },
